{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And He will love you</b> — in the merit of Abraham, concerning whom it is written: \"the seed of Abraham My lover\" (Isaiah 41:8)." "<b>And He will bless you</b> — in the merit of Isaac, concerning whom it is written: \"And Elohim blessed Isaac\" (Genesis 25:11)." "<b>And He will multiply you</b> — in the merit of Jacob, concerning whom it is written: \"be fruitful and multiply\" (Genesis 35:11). The verse begins with vav and ends with kaf — and likewise, \"And may the Elohim give you of the dew of heaven\" (Genesis 27:28) — the blessings with which Isaac blessed Jacob begin with vav and end with kaf, that all those blessings should be yours."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:03.055189220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}